+issueNumber: MDL-89296
+notes:
+  core:
+    - message: >-
+        A new `\core\output\renderer_base::react_component()` method has been
+        added to generate the mount point for a React component. Callers only
+        need to provide the component specifier and its props; serialisation,
+        escaping, and the DOM contract used by the React autoinit system are
+        handled internally.
+      type: improved
+    - message: >-
+        A new `\core\output\react_renderable` interface has been added. When a
+        renderable implementing it is passed to `render()`, the React component
+        it names is mounted using the props from `export_for_react()`. It takes
+        precedence over `named_templatable` and `templatable`, but a
+        `render_[renderable]` method in the renderer still takes precedence.
+      type: improved
